From: Sisyphus Aeolides <SisyphusAeolides@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 10:28:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mdadm: Skip missing legacy_async_del_gendisk parameter

On some kernels (e.g. 5.14.0-570.32.1.el9_6), mdadm-4.4-4.el9_7 fails 
to assemble arrays because it attempts to open 
/sys/module/md_mod/parameters/legacy_async_del_gendisk which does 
not exist, as the kernel never merged that parameter.

This patch gracefully checks if the parameter exists before attempting 
to open and write to it, preventing array assembly failures.

Signed-off-by: Sisyphus Aeolides <SisyphusAeolides@pm.me>
---
 util.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/util.c b/util.c
--- a/util.c
+++ b/util.c
@@ -2568,6 +2568,11 @@ bool set_md_mod_parameter(const char *name, const char *value)
 
 	snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "/sys/module/md_mod/parameters/%s", name);
 
+	if (access(path, F_OK) != 0) {
+		/* Parameter does not exist in this kernel, nothing to set. */
+		return true;
+	}
+
 	fd = open(path, O_WRONLY);
 	if (fd < 0) {
 		pr_err("Can't open %s\n", path);
--
2.43.0
